\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Full modelling framework. Centre: estimation on HHTS microdata and application to the 3.8-million-person synthetic population through Stages~0--7 (5a mode, 5 destination with PLC-captivity and M3 schedule-set arms, 5b detour-feasible trip destinations, 6 predict-only validation, 7 parking) to DynusT/MATSim-ready plans. Left rail: tour level (Stages~0--5, tour mode and destination choice) versus trip level (Stages~5b--6, intermediate-stop destinations and trip-chain validation). Left: data inputs. Right: the P1 crash chain (segments, SPF search, Empirical Bayes, OD accumulation) feeding the crash skim into Stage~5 and home crash-accessibility upstream. Bottom: the P2 SparseEA-AGDS search rail specifying every stage versus the P0 ActivitySim fixed baseline; shared calibration $\mathcal  {K}$ and the validation block implementing the M0-vs-P2 error comparison. Dashed grey: skim-feedback loop.}}{20}{figure.caption.3}\protected@file@percent }
\providecommand*\caption@xref[2]{\@setref\relax\@undefined{#1}}
\newlabel{fig:pipeline}{{1}{20}{Full modelling framework. Centre: estimation on HHTS microdata and application to the 3.8-million-person synthetic population through Stages~0--7 (5a mode, 5 destination with PLC-captivity and M3 schedule-set arms, 5b detour-feasible trip destinations, 6 predict-only validation, 7 parking) to DynusT/MATSim-ready plans. Left rail: tour level (Stages~0--5, tour mode and destination choice) versus trip level (Stages~5b--6, intermediate-stop destinations and trip-chain validation). Left: data inputs. Right: the P1 crash chain (segments, SPF search, Empirical Bayes, OD accumulation) feeding the crash skim into Stage~5 and home crash-accessibility upstream. Bottom: the P2 SparseEA-AGDS search rail specifying every stage versus the P0 ActivitySim fixed baseline; shared calibration $\mathcal {K}$ and the validation block implementing the M0-vs-P2 error comparison. Dashed grey: skim-feedback loop}{figure.caption.3}{}}
